BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Castleton Colonial Day Historic House Tour
DTSTART:20260815T100000
DTEND:20260815T150000
DTSTAMP:20260815T114232Z
UID:535422bc4161aff9e5db146a080b79@vermont-events
DESCRIPTION:Castleton Colonial Day Historic House Tour<br/>Step back in ti
 me as hostesses in Colonial attire greet guests in homes along Castleton h
 istoric Main Street during the 86th Annual Colonial Day Historic House Tou
 r\, Saturday August 15\, 2026. This annual event featuring over a dozen si
 tes throughout the village including outstanding period homes\, public bui
 ldings and historic sites.<br/>The Federated Church on Main Street\, descr
 ibed as builder Thomas Royal Dake’s architectural masterpiece\, is a pop
 ular stop on the tour. The pulpit\, with its intricate moldings and panels
  is one of the most extraordinary in the state. Dake is famous for his bea
 utifully scaled spiral staircases which can be seen in some of the homes o
 n the tour. <br/>There will be a quilt display at the Church as well.<br/>
 At the Higley House\, home of the Castleton Historical Society\, visitors 
 can tour the exhibits\, antique tools\, carriage collection and period fas
 hion display of 19th century clothing and accessories. On display at the H
 igley House will be the famous Blue Cat Quilt depicting historic landmarks
  in town and highlights from the book The Blue Cat of Castleton. The 2026 
 Castleton Colonial Day Historic House Tour will be held rain or shine Satu
 rday\, August 15th from 10am to 3pm. Tour tickets $25 can be purchased on 
 Colonial Day at ticket booths on Main Street. For information visit websit
 e at www.castletonhistorichousetour.org or call 802-468-5691. <br/>\n\nSou
 rces: Vermont Public
LOCATION:Location: Addison/Rutland
URL:https://www.vermontpublic.org/vermont-events-calendar/event/castleton-
 colonial-day-historic-house-tour-26-04-2026-13-47-55
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Fanny's Day: Historical Reenactment & Family Fun Day
DTSTART:20260815T113000
DTEND:20260815T123000
DTSTAMP:20260815T114232Z
UID:8b04533485bf304481fac201fc3b73@vermont-events
DESCRIPTION:Meet Fanny reenactors in the historic Allen House and in Fanny
 's Garden\, learn about life for women on the Homestead 250 years ago\, pl
 us family-friendly crafts\, 18th-century toys\, costume corner\, our annua
 l flax harvest\, &amp\; more! <br/><br/>Day: Saturday August 16\, 2026<br/
 >Times:<br/>*Reenactors &amp\; family crafts 11am-2pm<br/>*Flax harvest 11
 :30am-12:30pm<br/>*Museum open 10am-4pm<br/><br/>Location: Ethan Allen Hom
 estead Museum in Burlington\, VT<br/><br/>Admission: FREE (all reenactment
 s are free for America's 250th!)\n\nSources: Vermont Public
LOCATION:America 250
URL:https://www.vermontpublic.org/vermont-events-calendar/event/fannys-day
 -historical-reenactment-amp-family-fun-day-06-08-2026-13-12-59
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Ferrisburgh Volunteer Fire Department Chicken BBQ
DTSTART:20260815T163000
DTEND:20260815T183000
DTSTAMP:20260815T114232Z
UID:afde5fa5ab7b6137c5a8b2756e0c78@vermont-events
DESCRIPTION:Ferrisburgh Volunteer Fire Department will be hosting our annu
 al Chicken BBQ fundraiser. This will be TAKE OUT ONLY. This event will occ
 ur on 08/15/2026 and serving for take out will start at 4:30 PM. It is fir
 st come first serve! Meals price will be $18 dollars apiece\, and included
  will be 1/2 chicken\, side of coleslaw and baked beans\, cookie\, and a r
 oll. We appreciate the support and look forward to continuing to provide f
 ire service to the town of Ferrisburgh and surrounding towns.\n\nSources: 
 Vermont Public
LOCATION:Location: Addison/Rutland
URL:https://www.vermontpublic.org/vermont-events-calendar/event/ferrisburg
 h-volunteer-fire-department-chicken-bbq-02-07-2026-11-55-37
