BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Jamaica Day 2026
DTSTART:20260815T090000
DTEND:20260815T180000
DTSTAMP:20260815T114232Z
UID:ec9079ffd3355812f145c84a9758c6@vermont-events
DESCRIPTION:Hosted by the Jamaica Historical Foundation\, Jamaica Day carr
 ies on the cherished tradition of Old Home Days\, bringing neighbors\, for
 mer residents\, and visitors together for a day of small-town celebration.
 <br/><br/>Spend the day enjoying:<br/><br/>☼ A festive community parade<
 br/>☼ Live music throughout the day<br/>☼ Local food and craft vendors
 <br/>☼ A quilt show and raffle<br/>☼ Children's activities and games<b
 r/>☼ Historical exhibits and demonstrations<br/>☼ Free cake and a town
 -wide community photo<br/>☼ And much more!<br/><br/>Whether you're a lon
 gtime local or visiting for the weekend\, Jamaica Day is a chance to celeb
 rate the people\, history\, and traditions that make Jamaica\, Vermont suc
 h a special place.<br/><br/>Join us as we celebrate Jamaica's past\, prese
 nt\, and future!\n\nSources: Vermont Public
LOCATION:Fairs\, Festivals & Markets
URL:https://www.vermontpublic.org/vermont-events-calendar/event/jamaica-da
 y-2026-13-07-2026-14-36-02
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Rake Factory Arts Festival
DTSTART:20260815T120000
DTEND:20260815T220000
DTSTAMP:20260815T114232Z
UID:a608c1fe997adce717d35f3e6a68c0@vermont-events
DESCRIPTION:Enjoy music\, art\, food\, drink\, and natural beauty at the f
 irst annual Rake Factory Arts Festival! Local acts include Alex Homan and 
 Strayhound. Regional musical acts include DiTrani Brothers\, Good Judgemen
 t\, Kimaya Diggs\, Penelope Voss\, and Georgia Turman. Styles range from b
 luegrass and folk to pop and punk. Puppeteer Madison J. Cripps and toy-the
 ater duo Andy Colpitts &amp\; Seth Koproski will perform periodically thro
 ughout the day. During the afternoon\, local artists and craftspeople will
  sell prints\, paintings\, and posters. Middle Son Tattoo proprietor Caleb
  Colpitts and guest artist Owen Payette McGarry will offer on-site flash t
 attoos. Food and beverages will be sold on site by Tacos Del Reino and Sam
 's Listening Bar.\n\nSources: Vermont Public
LOCATION:Location: Northeast Kingdom
URL:https://www.vermontpublic.org/vermont-events-calendar/event/rake-facto
 ry-arts-festival-08-08-2026-12-41-00
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Shelburne Day at Farmers Market
DTSTART:20260815T090000
DTEND:20260815T140000
DTSTAMP:20260815T114232Z
UID:b3817ebd62c6c67fea17480d6d2499@vermont-events
DESCRIPTION:Shelburne Day is an oversize Farmers Market\, on the parade gr
 ounds\, the village green and in front of many of our shops. Come down for
  locally grown veggies\, handmade crafts\, an outdoor yoga class\, music\,
  outdoor sales and more. Come join in the fun!\n\nSources: Vermont Public
LOCATION:Fairs\, Festivals & Markets
URL:https://www.vermontpublic.org/vermont-events-calendar/event/shelburne-
 day-at-farmers-market-30-07-2026-10-59-37
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Single Signature Bookbinding
DTSTART:20260815T100000
DTEND:20260815T130000
DTSTAMP:20260815T114232Z
UID:19634a32d17c9a748f8ea412f90149@vermont-events
DESCRIPTION:In this beginner-level workshop\, you'll learn how to construc
 t a single-signature book with a hard cover. You'll learn basic book bindi
 ng techniques that will enable you to start creating unique books to use f
 or journaling\, sketches\, poems\, photos\, and more. We'll add a couple o
 f pockets on the inside\, and you can finish the book off with beads or a 
 design of your choice on the front. You'll have a variety of papers to cho
 ose from for your cover\, or you can bring some of your favorite papers.\n
 \nSources: Vermont Public
LOCATION:Classes & Workshops
URL:https://www.vermontpublic.org/vermont-events-calendar/event/single-sig
 nature-bookbinding-01-07-2026-14-06-48
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Splash Dance: Skipipop
DTSTART:20260815T130000
DTEND:20260815T150000
DTSTAMP:20260815T114232Z
UID:c03c74a34d9897c09098b1877fa590@vermont-events
DESCRIPTION:Performing as Skipipop\, Burlington-based DJ Sarah Umphlett de
 livers an electropop\, techno\, and speed house set inspired by her love f
 or experimental sounds and boundary-pushing artists. Her performance insta
 llation Material Feedback\, a first foray into non-traditional DJing where
  she cycled and manipulated feedback through her body and back into a soun
 dboard. Skipipop has performed b2b sets with Kate Kush at Radio Bean\, bec
 ome a regular behind the decks at Einsteins\, and organized and performed 
 at "Dance for Your Neighbor\," a successful ICE OUT benefit event at SEABA
 . <br/><br/>Delighted kids and their caregivers soak up some serious summe
 r fun with a DJ-fueled dance party in City Hall Park's interactive\, wheel
 chair accessible splash fountain. <br/><br/>Summer in the City is made pos
 sible in part thanks to Underwriters at the Pomerleau Family Foundation\; 
 Supporters Burlington Telecom\, Myti\, Soundtoys\, and Lake Champlain Choc
 olates\, and Community Partner American Flatbread Burlington &amp\; Mother
 ship Brewery. Media Sponsors: Seven Days and WCAX.⁠\n\nSources: Vermont 
 Public
LOCATION:Music: Rock\, Folk\, Jazz and More
URL:https://www.vermontpublic.org/vermont-events-calendar/event/splash-dan
 ce-skipipop-19-06-2026-20-20-17
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Wild & Scenic Film Festival
DTSTART:20260815T150000
DTEND:20260815T210000
DTSTAMP:20260815T114232Z
UID:7535243f0080dce770ba1f8ece58f9@vermont-events
DESCRIPTION:BigTown Projects will host the 2026 Wild &amp\; Scenic Film Fe
 stival on Saturday\, August 15th in Rochester\, Vermont. The event feature
 s the festival’s Best of the Fest 2026 touring program\, celebrating env
 ironmental activism\, outdoor culture\, and storytelling through film. Thi
 s year’s lineup includes the Vermont-made\, award-winning film Best Day 
 Ever\, directed by Ben Knight and recipient of the festival’s 2026 “Mo
 bilize” Award.<br/><br/>Screenings begin at 3:00 PM at the Valley Hub an
 d will be followed by a community discussion focused on adaptive recreatio
 n\, trail access\, and the future of inclusive outdoor experiences in Verm
 ont. Participating organizations include Ridgeline Outdoor Collective\, VT
  Huts &amp\; Trails\, VMBA\, Catamount Trail Association\, and Vermont Ada
 ptive Ski &amp\; Sports.<br/><br/>Following the screenings\, guests are in
 vited to gather at BigTown Vermont for the “Spirit of the Dough” wood-
 fired pizza dinner beginning at 6:00 PM. Tickets are available to purchase
  on our website via Eventive. Adult tickets are $35 for the screenings and
  $40 for the pizza dinner. Children under 12 attend the films free\; dinne
 r tickets for children are $20\; family of 4 deal offers free food to kids
  in a family of four.<br/><br/>A raffle supporting BigTown Projects will i
 nclude $500 credit to Green Mountain Bikes\, a stay at the Stable Inn\, gi
 ft certificates from participating organizations\, among other prizes from
  area businesses like Lawsons Beer. <br/><br/>For full exhibition\, worksh
 op\, and festival details\, visit bigtownvermont.com.\n\nSources: Vermont 
 Public
LOCATION:Film
URL:https://www.vermontpublic.org/vermont-events-calendar/event/wild-sceni
 c-film-festival-10-08-2026-15-35-54
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:You're a Good Man\, Charlie Brown
DTSTART:20260815T140000
DTEND:20260815T153000
DTSTAMP:20260815T114232Z
UID:f21ae91defa25376d996834cfcd1d3@vermont-events
DESCRIPTION:Based on the beloved Peanuts comic strip by Charles M. Schulz\
 , this charming musical brings Charlie Brown\, Snoopy\, Lucy\, Linus\, and
  the rest of the gang to life in a heartwarming celebration of friendship\
 , imagination\, and the joys of everyday life.<br/><br/><br/><br/>This pro
 duction will be performed outdoors in a partially shaded area. Chair seati
 ng will be available\; however\, a reservation does not guarantee a chair.
  Audience members are encouraged to bring a blanket or lawn chair for thei
 r comfort.<br/><br/>\n\nSources: Vermont Public
LOCATION:Kids & Family
URL:https://www.vermontpublic.org/vermont-events-calendar/event/youre-a-go
 od-man-charlie-brown-21-07-2026-15-07-07
END:VEVENT
